    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8f389729218393de05db70c885291e037b2623fd61b06f6f987095dbdb51ac1d",
      "text": "From early morning, explore the Roraima Tepui plateau. Accompanied by a guide, trek through intricate rock formations and canyons with extraordinary mountain vegetation. The highland tropics are sprinkled with quartz crystals.\n\nDuring the rainy season, lagoon pools form between rocks, home to endemic black frogs found only on Roraima. Almost everywhere grows the cosmic flower “Stegolepis guianensis”, with dense fan-like leaves and conical blooms. Nearly half of the plant species, including some orchids, are unique to the tepui. Return to the camp for dinner and overnight in tents.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast, lunch, dinner",
